Bluetooth: Controller: reset incompat when a peripheral CPR is rejected

A peripheral that sends LL_CONNECTION_PARAM_REQ sets the remote incompat
state to INCOMPAT_RESOLVABLE. If the central answers with
LL_REJECT_EXT_IND (e.g. 0x3b, as macOS does) or LL_UNKNOWN_RSP, the
procedure completes without resetting it, so the stale state lasts for
the rest of the connection. Later, any remote instant procedure (e.g.
LL_CHANNEL_MAP_IND) that arrives while some local procedure is active
(e.g. LE Ping) takes the "peripheral collision" path, which clears the
local procedure's rx_opcode; its response (LL_PING_RSP) is then expected
by neither procedure and the link is dropped with 0x24 (LMP PDU not
allowed). The central-side reject path already resets it.

--- a/subsys/bluetooth/controller/ll_sw/ull_llcp_conn_upd.c
+++ b/subsys/bluetooth/controller/ll_sw/ull_llcp_conn_upd.c
@@ -618,12 +618,16 @@
 		ctx->state = LP_CU_STATE_WAIT_INSTANT;
 		break;
 	case LP_CU_EVT_UNKNOWN:
+		/* CPR is over; release the collision state set when it was sent */
+		llcp_rr_set_incompat(conn, INCOMPAT_NO_COLLISION);
 		/* Unsupported in peer, so disable locally for this connection */
 		feature_unmask_features(conn, LL_FEAT_BIT_CONN_PARAM_REQ);
 		ctx->data.cu.error = BT_HCI_ERR_UNSUPP_REMOTE_FEATURE;
 		lp_cu_ntf_complete(conn, ctx, evt, param);
 		break;
 	case LP_CU_EVT_REJECT:
+		/* CPR is over; release the collision state set when it was sent */
+		llcp_rr_set_incompat(conn, INCOMPAT_NO_COLLISION);
 		ctx->data.cu.error = pdu->llctrl.reject_ext_ind.error_code;
 		lp_cu_ntf_complete(conn, ctx, evt, param);
 		break;
